This is a NEON blocked scan, which I have not compiled or run. At n = 16M the work is probably limited by memory bandwidth (128 MB read, 128 MB written), so I kept the vector code simple.

- **Within a block:** each iteration loads 8 elements as four 2-lane vectors. Each vector gets its own 2-lane scan, using `vextq_s64` against zero to shift by one lane and then an add. The totals of earlier vectors are broadcast and added into the later ones. This chain does not depend on the running carry.
- **Across blocks:** the only loop-carried dependency is one vector add of the block total into the carry. The carry is then added to the four results before they are stored.
- **Tail:** the last `n % 8` elements use a scalar loop that continues from the carry. Empty and tiny sizes fall through to this loop.
- **Memory:** no extra buffers are used.

<answer>
```c
#include <arm_neon.h>

void prefix_sum_i64(const int64_t *in, int64_t *out, size_t n)
{
    size_t i = 0;
    int64x2_t zero = vdupq_n_s64(0);
    int64x2_t carry = zero;
    for (; i + 8 <= n; i += 8) {
        int64x2_t v0 = vld1q_s64(in + i);
        int64x2_t v1 = vld1q_s64(in + i + 2);
        int64x2_t v2 = vld1q_s64(in + i + 4);
        int64x2_t v3 = vld1q_s64(in + i + 6);
        int64x2_t s0 = vaddq_s64(v0, vextq_s64(zero, v0, 1));
        int64x2_t s1 = vaddq_s64(v1, vextq_s64(zero, v1, 1));
        int64x2_t s2 = vaddq_s64(v2, vextq_s64(zero, v2, 1));
        int64x2_t s3 = vaddq_s64(v3, vextq_s64(zero, v3, 1));
        s1 = vaddq_s64(s1, vdupq_laneq_s64(s0, 1));
        s2 = vaddq_s64(s2, vdupq_laneq_s64(s1, 1));
        s3 = vaddq_s64(s3, vdupq_laneq_s64(s2, 1));
        int64x2_t total = vdupq_laneq_s64(s3, 1);
        vst1q_s64(out + i,     vaddq_s64(s0, carry));
        vst1q_s64(out + i + 2, vaddq_s64(s1, carry));
        vst1q_s64(out + i + 4, vaddq_s64(s2, carry));
        vst1q_s64(out + i + 6, vaddq_s64(s3, carry));
        carry = vaddq_s64(carry, total);
    }
    int64_t c = vgetq_lane_s64(carry, 0);
    for (; i < n; i++) {
        c += in[i];
        out[i] = c;
    }
}
```
